---
/**
 * Asks once per browser whether the Google map may load.
 *
 * Hidden until src/scripts/consent.ts decides it is needed - so without JavaScript it
 * never appears, which is correct: without JavaScript the map never loads either, and
 * there is nothing to consent to.
 *
 * Accept and reject are visually identical on purpose. A refusal that is harder to find
 * than an agreement is not a choice, and the law that requires the question also requires
 * that the two answers cost the same.
 *
 * **The wording is the sibling site's, word for word** (alpaki-kazimierzdolny.pl), on the
 * owner's instruction in October 2026 - the title, the paragraph and "Akceptuję". Every claim
 * in it was checked against this site before it was copied: no statistics and no cookies of our
 * own (the decision lives in `localStorage`), the map is the only third-party element (the
 * Facebook block is self-hosted - § 5 of the privacy policy), and "Ustawienia mapy" in the
 * footer is where the consent is withdrawn. If any of the three stops being true, this text
 * becomes false, not merely different from the sibling's.
 */
---

<aside id="consent" class="consent" hidden aria-label="Zgoda na treści zewnętrzne">
  <div class="consent__text">
    <p class="consent__title">Mapa Google i pliki cookie</p>
    <p>
      Ta strona nie prowadzi statystyk i nie zapisuje własnych plików cookie. Jedynym elementem
      zewnętrznym jest mapa dojazdu Google - jej wyświetlenie przekazuje tej firmie Państwa adres IP
      i pozwala jej zapisać własne pliki cookie. Zgodę można wycofać w stopce; szczegóły opisuje <a
        href="/polityka-prywatnosci/">polityka prywatności</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="consent__actions">
    <button type="button" data-consent="accept">Akceptuję</button>
    <button type="button" data-consent="reject">Odrzucam</button>
  </div>
</aside>

<style>
  .consent {
    /* The bar holds the site's only link on this ground, and the default --green is 2.63:1
       against it - under the 3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 asks of a focus indicator. --green-lit gives
       9.49:1. `.footer`, `.history` and `.lightbox` each raise it in the same one line. */
    --focus-ring: var(--green-lit);
    position: fixed;
    inset-inline: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    /* The same ground as the lightbox, and derived from the token for the same reason it is
       derived there: this was written out as `rgb(35 40 31 / 92%)`, which is the **old** --ink
       (#23281F), so when the 2a theme moved --ink to #1F2A21 the bar quietly stopped matching
       the footer it is meant to belong to. The fallback on the line above is the same token at
       full opacity, for browsers without color-mix - worse looking, but never a see-through bar
       over a scrolling page. */
    background: var(--ink);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 92%, transparent);
    color: var(--footer-body);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--footer-rule);
    padding: 0.9rem var(--edge);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  }

  /* `display: flex` above is an author style, and any author `display` beats the
     `display: none` the browser attaches to [hidden] - so without this rule the bar ignored
     its own `hidden` attribute entirely: it stood on all ten pages, including the seven that
     embed nothing, and it did not go away when either button was pressed, because
     `hideBanner()` in src/scripts/consent.ts hides it by setting exactly that attribute.
     `.lightbox` in global.css and three selectors in Compositions.astro carry the same rule
     for the same reason; this component was the one that did not. */
  .consent[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .consent__text {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    max-width: 72ch;
    flex: 1 1 22rem;
    color: var(--footer-body);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  /* An overline, so it is ochre - the one place that accent is allowed (CLAUDE.md), and on a
     dark ground the lit variant, as on the footer. */
  .consent__title {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ochre-lit);
  }

  /* Not the prose green of `.copy a`: this ground is dark, and --green-lit is the accent the
     rest of the dark plates use. */
  .consent__text a {
    color: var(--green-lit);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .consent__text a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .consent__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
  }

  /* Identical, down to the last pixel. Do not make one of them quieter. */
  .consent button {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bone);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid rgb(238 240 230 / 28%);
    padding-inline: 1.1rem;
    min-height: var(--tap);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .consent button:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--green-lit);
    border-color: var(--green-lit);
  }
</style>
